stdout | test/formats/effects-drift.test.ts > the drift row seeds, converts and refuses > refuses zero, everything that rounds to zero, and everything out of range
--- driftPxPerFrameRefusal ---
0                      REFUSED  (zero: indistinguishable from none in ROM)
    0 is not a drift rate. A layer that should not drift spells "none". It is indistinguishable from no drift at all in ROM, and aeon refuses it at build time.
0.001                  REFUSED  (rounds to zero on the wire)
    0.001 px/frame is 0 in wire units (1 px/frame = 256). 0 is not a drift rate. A layer that should not drift spells "none". It is indistinguishable from no drift at all in ROM, and aeon refuses it at build time.
-0.001                 REFUSED  (rounds to zero, leftward)
    -0.001 px/frame is 0 in wire units (1 px/frame = 256). 0 is not a drift rate. A layer that should not drift spells "none". It is indistinguishable from no drift at all in ROM, and aeon refuses it at build time.
0.00390625             ACCEPTED (one wire unit: the slowest legal)
    
-16                    ACCEPTED (the bound itself)
    
16                     ACCEPTED (the bound itself)
    
-16.01                 REFUSED  (past the bound, leftward)
    -16.01 px/frame is outside the contract's -16..16 px/frame. -16.01 px/frame is -4099 in wire units, against a -4096..4096 bound (1 px/frame = 256). That is a TASTE bound, not a correctness one; raise it in the contract rather than working around it.
16.01                  REFUSED  (past the bound)
    16.01 px/frame is outside the contract's -16..16 px/frame. 16.01 px/frame is 4099 in wire units, against a -4096..4096 bound (1 px/frame = 256). That is a TASTE bound, not a correctness one; raise it in the contract rather than working around it.
35.15625               REFUSED  (the generator forwards Rate(9000))
    35.15625 px/frame is outside the contract's -16..16 px/frame. In the file that is 9000, against a -4096..4096 bound (1 px/frame = 256). That is a TASTE bound, not a correctness one; raise it in the contract rather than working around it.
NaN                    REFUSED  (not a number)
    NaN is not a drift rate: type a signed number of pixels per frame.
0.125                  ACCEPTED (AIZ1 clouds)
    
6                      ACCEPTED (the corpus maximum)
    

